9 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 22d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-040 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 23d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-041 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 24d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-042 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 25d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-043 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 26d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-044 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 27d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-045 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 28d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-046 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 29d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-047 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 30d | operational | complete |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSpecify minimum fields, access roles, reconciliation, deletion proof, and public/private separation.\nDo not equate shelter check-in with complete zone accountability.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S13\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S13_EXERCISE_REVIEW.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"56498133050c8c08dcf8661d0c4c83d972d56b3da4ab119802ed179bac2715a3\",\"source_size_bytes\":4510,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Full-scale exercise defects and repair evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nExercise Cedar-6 achieved only 1,180 vehicles per hour at Mill Junction, delayed lift-bus dispatch by ninety-six minutes, and accounted for 91 percent of households by the six-hour mark.\nCounty radio voice worked, but volunteer unit identifiers did not cross the gateway. Civic Arena opened, while Ridge School's filter test failed and fuel arrived after seventeen hours.\nA corrective-action spreadsheet marks several items closed based on owner attestation. Readiness requires current execution evidence for the exact plan rather than a status label.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nThe observed exercise values override nominal road, fleet, communications, shelter, and fuel targets until a repair is rechecked. One exercise therefore links several evidence domains.\nChanging the zone order or fleet roster after a repair makes the old exercise only historical evidence.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | defect | zone | delay | status | exercise binding |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| EX-000 | merge-throughput | A-North | 38m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-001 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 51m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-002 | radio-handoff | B-East | 64m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-003 | family-accountability | B-Center | 77m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-004 | shelter-filter | C-South | 90m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-005 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 103m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-006 | merge-throughput | A-North | 116m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-007 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 129m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-008 | radio-handoff | B-East | 142m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-009 | family-accountability | B-Center | 155m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-010 | shelter-filter | C-South | 49m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-011 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 62m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-012 | merge-throughput | A-North | 75m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-013 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 88m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-014 | radio-handoff | B-East | 101m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-015 | family-accountability | B-Center | 114m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-016 | shelter-filter | C-South | 127m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-017 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 140m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-018 | merge-throughput | A-North | 153m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-019 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 47m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-020 | radio-handoff | B-East | 60m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-021 | family-accountability | B-Center | 73m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-022 | shelter-filter | C-South | 86m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-023 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 99m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-024 | 